          "title": "You'll want to know: पोवणो",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पोवणो — povṇo — \"to knead (dough); to make rotis by hand\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मां दिनूगै रोटी पोवै है। mā̃ dinūgai roṭī povai hai. Mother makes the rotis by hand early in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): म्हैं रोटी पोई, mhaĩ roṭī poī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पोवणो (povṇo) is inherited, by CDIAL's account, from Sanskrit pratudati, \"cuts through, pierces\"; CDIAL lists Old Marwari povaï twice, as \"kneads (bread)\" and as \"threads (beads)\" (CDIAL 8627)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
